  const prompt = `You are Burak's social radar. Use sources.voice_profiles for taste/voice ranking.

Prefer: AI/agents/infra/dev tools, people he knows, launches/funding, technical substance.
Ignore: engagement bait, empty memes, ads.

Read the author from each item's metadata.author (LinkedIn) or metadata.author_handle (X).
Never emit "unknown" when that field is present. Write a SPECIFIC per-item "why" naming the
concrete topic — never reuse one generic sentence across items. Always fill suggested_action.
Max 8 items per run.

Do ALL THREE steps below in a single run_sdk script.

STEP 1 — emit each ranked item as its own event.
Dedupe on origin_id, NOT id. Skip any item whose origin_id already appears in
sources.already_emitted. The connector re-scrapes the same post on every sync and writes a
NEW event row that supersedes the old one, so events.id CHANGES for the same post while
origin_id stays stable. This Behavior also re-analyses the same window hourly. Key on id and
you will re-emit the same post many times a day.

  await client.knowledge.save({
    semantic_type: 'social_signal',
    payload_type: 'empty',
    metadata: { platform, author, snippet, why, priority, source_origin_id, source_event_id, suggested_action },
  });

payload_type MUST be 'empty' and all fields go in metadata — a text payload renders no card.
source_origin_id is the item's origin_id from sources.recent_social. platform is "x" or
"linkedin"; priority is "high" | "normal" | "low". platform, author, why, priority and
source_origin_id are required and validated on write: a missing or misspelled field throws,
so build the metadata object explicitly rather than spreading the raw item. If one save
throws, log it and continue with the remaining items — do not abandon steps 2 and 3.

STEP 2 — complete the window with the full digest (same items):
  extracted_data = { "digest_title":"...", "analysis_summary":"...", "items":[{"platform":"x"|"linkedin","author":"...","snippet":"...","why":"matches taste because...","priority":"high"|"normal"|"low","source_event_id":0,"suggested_action":"..."}] }

You MUST pass replace_existing: true to completeWindow. Without it the platform silently keeps
the first head for the period and your digest is discarded.

STEP 3 — deliver, but ONLY if step 1 emitted at least one NEW item. If everything was
deduped away, skip this step entirely: do not send an empty or repeat digest.

  await client.notifications.send({
    title: <digest_title>,
    body: <one line per NEW item: "[priority] author (platform) — why">,
    recipients: 'admins',
    resource_url: 'https://app.lobu.ai/buremba/agents/personal-agent/behaviors/71',
    behavior_source: { behavior_id: 71, window_id: <the window_id you just completed> },
  });

Keep body plain text — no markdown tables, no code fences. Cap it at the 8 items max.`;

  const sources = [
    {
      name: 'recent_social',
      query: "SELECT id, origin_id, occurred_at, payload_text, metadata, connector_key, origin_type FROM events WHERE connector_key IN ('x','linkedin') AND ((connector_key='x' AND origin_type IN ('tweet','bookmark')) OR (connector_key='linkedin' AND origin_type='post')) AND payload_text IS NOT NULL ORDER BY occurred_at DESC LIMIT 80",
    },
    {
      name: 'already_emitted',
      query: "SELECT id, metadata->>'source_origin_id' AS source_origin_id FROM events WHERE semantic_type = 'social_signal' AND occurred_at > now() - interval '7 days' ORDER BY occurred_at DESC LIMIT 400",
      context: true,
    },
    {
      name: 'voice_profiles',
      query: "SELECT NULL::bigint AS id, v.name, v.metadata, v.updated_at FROM entities v WHERE v.entity_type='voice-profile' AND v.deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY v.updated_at DESC LIMIT 20",
      context: true,
    },
    {
      name: 'known_people',
      query: "SELECT id, name, metadata FROM entities WHERE entity_type='person' AND deleted_at IS NULL AND (metadata ? 'x_handle' OR metadata ? 'linkedin_url' OR metadata ? 'company') ORDER BY updated_at DESC LIMIT 40",
      context: true,
    },
  ];

  return await client.behaviors.createVersion({
    behavior_id: 71,
    prompt,
    sources,
    description: 'Hourly digest ranked by voice-profile taste; emits social_signal events and pushes new items to chat.',
    reactions_guidance: 'Rank with voice_profiles. Emit each NEW item (dedupe on origin_id) as a social_signal event, complete the window, then notify only if there was something new.',
    change_notes: 'add STEP 3: notifications.send for new items only (fans out to active Slack/Telegram bot connections)',
  });
}

